WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:03.586
In industries where

00:00:03.586 --> 00:00:06.381
there aren't people that
look like you,

00:00:06.381 --> 00:00:08.633
go where you don't belong
because one day you will.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:11.678
When we started our business,

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:14.055
we definitely were faced
with extra challenges,

00:00:14.055 --> 00:00:15.015
some biases.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:17.642
We had a lot of pushback
as to whether or not

00:00:17.642 --> 00:00:19.644
Black women actually
even drink wine

00:00:19.644 --> 00:00:21.980
or if Black woman
could run a wine business.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.106
Of course, all of that

00:00:23.106 --> 00:00:25.191
sort of fueled
our passion and our mission

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.110
and really working to service

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.362
this consumer that we
felt we know so well

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:30.947
and deserved to be represented.

00:00:40.665 --> 00:00:43.001
Well, I think we have to
start with our sister story.

00:00:43.001 --> 00:00:43.793
Yes.

00:00:43.793 --> 00:00:45.837
Both of us were born in
Los Angeles

00:00:45.837 --> 00:00:47.380
to the same father.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.216
We grew up thinking
that we were only children

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.594
on completely different
sides of the world

00:00:52.594 --> 00:00:53.887
and different hemispheres.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:56.681
I grew up in Central Coast
of California in Monterey.

00:00:56.681 --> 00:00:58.099
She grew up in New Zealand.

00:00:58.099 --> 00:01:01.186
And even though we were
a world apart,

00:01:01.186 --> 00:01:04.355
we both grew up in really beautiful
agricultural areas.

00:01:04.355 --> 00:01:07.859
We both longed to be
winemakers

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:10.570
and we both actually
longed to have a sibling.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.656
We reunited in 1999.

00:01:13.656 --> 00:01:15.700
When I got the letter
and found out

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:16.951
that I had a little sister

00:01:16.951 --> 00:01:20.371
and I was like,
this really sounds very scammy.

00:01:20.371 --> 00:01:23.458
But I of course called the number
that was on the letter

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:26.586
and we actually made plans
to meet the next day.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.630
It changed my life forever.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:31.841
I just can't imagine
life without her now.

00:01:31.841 --> 00:01:33.009
Ohhh, awww.

00:01:36.888 --> 00:01:38.389
17 years later,

00:01:38.389 --> 00:01:40.850
we have a
multinational wine company

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.144
and we have a non-for-profit,

00:01:43.144 --> 00:01:45.230
the McBride Sisters
SHE CAN Fund.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.608
We have three brands,

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:50.401
the McBride Sisters
Collection Wines,

00:01:50.401 --> 00:01:52.445
which are our wines from
where I grew up

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.114
in the Central Coast of California.

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:56.658 position:63%
And in New Zealand where Andréa grew up,

00:01:56.658 --> 00:01:58.993
we have Black Girl Magic wines

00:01:58.993 --> 00:02:01.454
which are premium wines
from California.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:04.541
and we have SHE CAN wines,
which of course is our

00:02:04.541 --> 00:02:06.000
wines in a can.

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:08.545
SHE CAN wines,

00:02:08.545 --> 00:02:10.922
we launched in 2019.

00:02:10.922 --> 00:02:13.174
We wanted to
take that opportunity

00:02:13.174 --> 00:02:14.759
to give back.

00:02:14.759 --> 00:02:17.095
We've seen a lot of the struggles
that women were having

00:02:17.095 --> 00:02:18.054
in the industry.

00:02:18.054 --> 00:02:20.515
So we started our professional
development fund.

00:02:20.515 --> 00:02:21.641
Which would be scholarships,

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:24.352 position:66%
mentorships, grants for professional women

00:02:24.352 --> 00:02:25.436
in wine and spirits.

00:02:26.604 --> 00:02:29.524
2020 was a little bit
of a different year.

00:02:29.524 --> 00:02:33.027
The pandemic was starting
to take a hold of the world.

00:02:33.027 --> 00:02:35.738
We started to see some really
disturbing numbers

00:02:35.738 --> 00:02:37.866
around the federal funding,

00:02:37.866 --> 00:02:39.951
the PPP grants that
were going to businesses.

00:02:39.951 --> 00:02:41.536
And we started to learn

00:02:41.536 --> 00:02:44.122
that Black-owned businesses,
one, were shuttering

00:02:44.122 --> 00:02:46.833
at a much faster rate
than any other

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:50.962
and that 96% of the businesses
either didn't qualify

00:02:50.962 --> 00:02:53.965
or were rejected for
the PPP funding.

00:02:53.965 --> 00:02:55.091
And we decided that year

00:02:55.091 --> 00:02:58.011
that we were going
to award cash grants

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.554
to Black women owned businesses.

00:02:59.554 --> 00:03:01.598
And then we had
some amazing support

00:03:01.598 --> 00:03:03.850
from corporate donors as well

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.810
that also were able to provide

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:07.687
professional services
to these businesses,

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:10.231 position:61%
assistance with financial planning, HR,

00:03:10.231 --> 00:03:11.524
and employee management

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:12.984
that some of these
businesses might need

00:03:12.984 --> 00:03:14.903
in such a challenging time.

00:03:14.903 --> 00:03:18.406 position:58%
This wine label is called Papatūānuku

00:03:18.406 --> 00:03:21.284 position:66%
which in Māori translates to Mother Earth.

00:03:21.284 --> 00:03:25.246
Pinot Noir is a very fickle,
hard grape to grow.

00:03:25.246 --> 00:03:26.748
It has thinner skin

00:03:26.748 --> 00:03:30.210
and really expresses the dirt
in which it's grown.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.462
The wine industry has had

00:03:32.462 --> 00:03:35.298
some version of wine education,
but it's been pretty dull.

00:03:36.007 --> 00:03:37.091
This is my favorite wine.

00:03:37.091 --> 00:03:39.969
We tried to create something
that would engage folks

00:03:39.969 --> 00:03:41.346
in a new way and help them

00:03:41.346 --> 00:03:42.972
remember what
they were learning.

00:03:42.972 --> 00:03:45.183
Super silky soft tannins.

00:03:45.183 --> 00:03:47.727
It just like coats
your whole mouth.

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:49.020
It has a really long finish

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.731
and there's really good
integration of flavor.

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:54.901
Traditionally, wine and
food pairings have been from

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:59.322
this quite Eurocentric standpoint,
duck confit and Chardonnay.

00:03:59.322 --> 00:04:00.657
And we integrated pop culture.

00:04:00.657 --> 00:04:02.992 position:63%
We integrated contemporary ways in which

00:04:02.992 --> 00:04:05.245
people like to eat and drink.

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:07.747
We're talking about
what goes with tacos.

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.332
We're talking about
wine and watch.

00:04:09.332 --> 00:04:12.335
What are you watching on Netflix
and what should you pair it with.

00:04:14.879 --> 00:04:16.256
Innovation really comes

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:18.758
and growth really comes
from diversity of thought.

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:21.844
So if you have people from all
different walks of life

00:04:21.844 --> 00:04:23.304
and backgrounds,
it doesn't matter

00:04:23.304 --> 00:04:24.305
what the problem is,

00:04:24.305 --> 00:04:26.391
everybody's going to approach it
and try and solve it

00:04:26.391 --> 00:04:27.684
in a different way.

00:04:27.684 --> 00:04:29.644 position:64%
And that's when the breakthroughs happen.

00:04:29.644 --> 00:04:31.980
And so I think because
the wine industry

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:33.564
hasn't been that diverse,

00:04:33.564 --> 00:04:35.608
there is so much opportunity.

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:37.485
And so we're
actually really optimistic

00:04:37.485 --> 00:04:39.445
and excited about the future.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:43.574
I think success for me will be

00:04:43.574 --> 00:04:46.369
when this industry

00:04:46.369 --> 00:04:49.455
fully represents
the world around us.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:50.206
Yes.

00:04:50.206 --> 00:04:52.500
That it's not
dominated by one gender

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.460
or one race of people,
that it really

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.962
is representing the consumer.

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:58.506
More people love wine
than ever before.

00:04:58.506 --> 00:05:00.758
So, when I can visually see that

00:05:00.758 --> 00:05:02.260
when we go out
in the world and that's

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:04.554
who's at our
industry conferences and

00:05:04.554 --> 00:05:06.556
who's at the
winemakers conferences,

00:05:06.556 --> 00:05:09.017
I'll feel that that's success.

